---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Disclaimer — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Palmistry Path is an educational resource. Content about palmistry is for personal reflection and study — not diagnosis, prediction, or professional advice."
		/>
		<style>
			main section {
				margin-bottom: 2.5em;
			}
			main h2 {
				font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3.5vw, 1.5em);
				margin-top: 2em;
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
				padding-bottom: 0.35em;
				border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(201, 169, 110, 0.15);
			}
			.updated {
				font-size: 0.8em;
				color: var(--color-text-muted);
				opacity: 0.65;
				margin-bottom: 2em;
			}
			.notice {
				padding: 1.25em 1.5em;
				border: 1px solid rgba(201, 169, 110, 0.22);
				border-radius: 6px;
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
				font-size: 0.9em;
				color: var(--color-text-muted);
				line-height: 1.75;
				margin-bottom: 2.5em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
			<h1>Disclaimer</h1>
			<p class="updated">Last updated: May 2026</p>

			<div class="notice">
				<em>
					Palmistry Path is for education, personal reflection, and exploration of a centuries-old
					interpretive tradition. It is not a substitute for professional medical, legal, financial,
					or psychological advice.
				</em>
			</div>

			<section>
				<h2>Palmistry as Education and Reflection</h2>
				<p>
					The content on this site presents palmistry as a structured interpretive tradition with
					deep cultural roots in Indian, Chinese, and Western practice. It is offered for personal
					study, self-reflection, and an appreciation of how different cultures have observed and
					interpreted the human hand.
				</p>
				<p>
					Palmistry is not a science. The interpretations described on this site are drawn from
					traditional sources and are presented as cultural and historical knowledge — not as
					verified facts about any individual's life, health, or future.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>No Diagnosis or Medical Claims</h2>
				<p>
					Nothing on Palmistry Path should be interpreted as medical advice or diagnosis. Certain
					palmistry traditions have historically associated hand features with states of health —
					these are recorded here as part of those traditions, not as medical guidance.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you have health concerns, speak with a qualified medical professional.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>No Predictive Guarantee</h2>
				<p>
					Palmistry Path makes no claim that palmistry predicts future events. Content that describes
					traditional interpretations of specific hand features — such as "the fate line is
					traditionally associated with career trajectory" — reflects what those traditions teach,
					not a guarantee of any outcome for any individual.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>No Legal or Financial Advice</h2>
				<p>
					Nothing on this site should be taken as legal, financial, or investment advice. For
					decisions in those areas, consult a qualified professional.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Accuracy of Traditional Sources</h2>
				<p>
					We aim to represent source traditions accurately and to attribute interpretations to their
					correct origins. Where traditions disagree, we note the disagreement rather than presenting
					one view as universal. If you believe something here is misattributed or inaccurate, please
					let us know via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
